Deliberate StimGate-Specific Modifications
-------------------------------------------
1. Header Redirection:
   Replaced FAUST-wide header dependencies with a minimal, package-local header
   `src/stimgate_faust.h` (via `src/faust.h`) containing only the structures and
   function signatures needed for `cpPmden`.
2. Outer Loop Safety Guard in `cpPmden.cpp`:
   Added a maximum-iteration count safety guard (`cpPmden_max_iter = 10000`) to the
   outer `while (stillRepeating)` loop in `src/cpPmden.cpp` to guarantee termination
   and prevent infinite loops on edge-case or near-uniform input data. This corresponds
   to the `MAXIT` parameter present in the original `ftnonpar` FORTRAN source `pmden.f`.
3. Degenerate Input Handling in `stimgate_cppmden.cpp`:
   Inputs with `n < 50` return a zero-density result of length `n - 1`, matching the
   Kuiper-bound lookup table lower bound in `cpPmden`.
4. No Algorithmic Alterations:
   Aside from the loop safety guard and header decoupling, no algorithmic changes
   were made to any ported function.
